{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe day has been a strange mix of history and hygiene. Here in Aachen, the sexton actually let me sit in Charlemagne’s own coronation chair. It was a curious sensation; one feels the weight of the state not as an abstraction, but as a physical seat. I spent the whole day with Bettendorf, examining his paintings until the light failed, and then walked out to Burtscheid for a sulphur bath. It is a strange remedy, but the water is hot and the air is sharp.\n\nI have since traveled to Liège, arriving late this evening. I am staying with a fellow passenger for the night. The journey is uneventful, but the mind is full. I miss the quiet of Berlin and your company. I shall continue north tomorrow. Give my love to the boys.\n\nYours,\nG. W. F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080252,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":187,"prompt_tokens":947,"total_tokens":1134,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-nVAfqLDP20DnxkVLhtq4lwYAznMZdEbo","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":947,"prompt_ms":922.228,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9738416050686377,"prompt_per_second":1026.8610365332652,"predicted_n":187,"predicted_ms":4476.26,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.065913978494624,"predicted_per_second":41.55254609875208}}